      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, this was done based on binder_alloc_new_buf_locked() code where:\n\n  data_offsets_size \u003d ALIGN(data_size, sizeof(void *)) + ALIGN(offsets_size, sizeof(void*));\n  size \u003d data_offsets_size + ALIGN(extra_buffers_size, sizeof(void *));\n\nSo the end of the buffer is at:\n  ALIGN(data_size, sizeof(void *)) +\n  ALIGN(offsets_size, sizeof(void *)) +\n  ALIGN(extra_buffers_size, sizeof(void *));\n\nWe added ALIGN(secctx_sz, sizeof(u64)) to extra_buffers_size to make room for this string. We aligned on sizeof(u64) because we know that extra_buffers_size has to be u64 aligned. This is tested in binder_transaction():\n\n  if (!IS_ALIGNED(extra_buffers_size, sizeof(u64))) {\n\nso since we added ALIGN(secctx_sz, sizeof(u64)), that\u0027s what is subtracted to find the beginning of the secctx string area, so we get:\n\n  ALIGN(data_size, sizeof(void *)) +\n  ALIGN(offsets_size, sizeof(void*)) +\n  ALIGN(extra_buffers_size, sizeof(void *) -\n  ALIGN(secctx_sz, sizeof(u64))\n\nwhere do you think I went wrong here?",
      "parentUuid": "494221b9_6fd6b786",
      "revId": "6991c2e9fa286b3ad35bda1e00ffb1b8cea5ccd5",
